   {"sections":[{"title":"5. Dated Catalysts","body":"No dated catalyst was admitted for this run. I was handed no calendar row carrying a time, a named event and a forecast or prior, so under the naming rule I decline to invent one: an event no dated source admitted would forfeit this section, and that applies even to a release everyone assumes is due. There is therefore no next admitted event to branch into A/B/C/D paths, no transmission order to assign, no base case to flag, and no confirmation/falsification pair to specify, because each of those must attach to a named, dated, sourced event. Reverse risk: the absence of an admitted row is itself the hazard — a real release could print inside this window unhedged by this section, so the desk should treat the catalyst calendar as unverified rather than empty until a dated source is supplied."}],"spyForecast":{"referenceClose":{"date":"2026-09-04","value":770.19},"t1Down":0.5,"t5Down":0.54}}
